<!-- The ird:* elements are IRD/BV-BRC extensions, not part of phyloXML.
     They are carried in the "urn:local:ird-extensions" namespace, which is
     what the schema's ##other wildcard is for, and they sit at the END of
     their parent because that wildcard comes last in the element sequence.

     The ird: PREFIX is deliberate rather than a default xmlns, and the reason
     is OUR reader rather than interop: the desktop reads either form.
     phyloxml.js has a hardcoded handler for the IRD element <flu_type>
     (APPTYPE), which assumes it appears BEFORE the clade, where these files
     used to put it and where the schema does not allow it. At the
     schema-required position there is no current object and the parse THROWS.
     The prefix makes the name stop matching that handler. If phyloxml.js ever
     becomes namespace-aware, or that handler is dropped, the prefix stops
     being necessary. -->
